venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
db.sqlite3
# Local snapshots taken before a destructive management command. Same client
# evidence as db.sqlite3, so they stay out of the repo the same way — the
# pattern above only matches the exact filename.
db.sqlite3.bak*
.env
.DS_Store
cookies.txt
*.json
# The gateway's example config is a template with no secret in it, so it is
# committed on purpose. The real gateway.json holds a device credential and
# stays ignored by the *.json rule above, exactly as it should.
!gateway.example.json
# The directory the platform writes provisioned configs into, and the folder a
# site syncs its exports into. Both are volumes in the deployment and are only
# ever populated on a machine running this locally. The configs inside hold
# live device credentials, so the whole directory stays out rather than relying
# on the *.json rule — which would still leave the atomic-write temp files.
gateway-config/
gateway-inbox/
*.log
_tmp_runserver.log
runserver.log
new_info.txt
apis/*.pdf
media/
*.backup
test video.png

*.gz
